-- title:
--   Batch source construction has a downset-based time bound
-- statement:
--   Let $c,h,J,t$ be natural numbers with $t\le W=512hJ$. Write $D(W,t)=\sum_{i=0}^{t}\binom Wi$, the number of binary masks of width $W$ and weight at most $t$. Let $F(h,J)$ be the explicit retained-source construction factor, containing polynomial dimension terms and logarithms of the local hash and endpoint bounds. Then the batch source constructor's operation budget obeys
--   $$
--   T_{\rm batch}(c,h,J,t)\le(c+1)\bigl(F(h,J)+720\bigr)\bigl(D(W,t)+1\bigr).
--   $$
--   The batch executes the retained-source host for $c$ catalog entries. This estimate includes the per-entry wrapper and fixed outer-loop overhead of the closed source-bank program.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBlockSourceBatchProgram.lean#L36-L58

